AB Generative Artificial Intelligence is revolutionizing economies, bridging gaps with advanced deep learning and natural language processing techniques. In India there are 22 scheduled languages. Top Large language models such as Chat-GPT supports only limited languages. On the other-hand AI4Bharat shows highly efficient Multilingual translation benchmarks. However, in prompt engineering, using LLM alone as a translator often leads to hallucinated outputs lacking context, defaulting to the most common meaning of words and producing extremely bookish language. Fine-tuning the LLM models to support all the languages is costly. This work explores the challenges in machine translation of native languages when using prompt engineering as well as the transformative role of an LLM with the AI4Bharat transformer as a sophisticated language interface, enabling seamless communication across Indic languages with remarkable translation quality. In this study, the performance of AI4Bharat transformers is evaluated using Samsung consumer electronics offers dataset. The proposed translation pipeline integrates IndicTrans2 and Mistral models to benchmark the translation accuracy. By selecting evaluation metrics that focus on translation quality and contextual accuracy, the limitations are addressed. Leveraging RAG Framework with Mistral and IndicTrans2, the approach enhances translation performance for sector-specific offers, demonstrating the effectiveness of specialized LLM prompts and transformers in improving multilingual translations. This research highlights the potential to advance linguistic interfaces and foster cross-cultural communication, reshaping the way translation across diverse linguistic communities is perceived and achieved.
