AB The article analyzes problems of deep learning (DL) approaches to natural language processing (NLP). The research covers various NLP tasks implemented with artificial neural networks (ANNs), convolutional neural networks (CNNs), and recurrent neural networks (RNNs). These architectures allow solving a wide range of natural language processing problems that previously did not lend themselves to effective solutions: sentence modeling, semantic role marking, named entity recognition, answering questions, text categorization, machine translation. Along with the advantages of using CNN for solving NLP problems, there are problems associated with many variable network parameters and the choice of its architecture. Authors propose an evolutionary algorithm for optimizing the architectures of convolutional neural networks, which has the advantage of a small population size of networks. It turned out to be important because, due to the complexity of CNN, it takes a long time to train one network. The experimental results showed that the proposed neuroevolutionary approach could quickly find an optimized CNN architecture for a given dataset with acceptable accuracy.
