AB This study presents a benchmarking analysis of the Qualcomm Cloud AI 100 Ultra (QAic) accelerator for large language model (LLM) inference, evaluating its energy efficiency (throughput per watt) and performance against leading NVIDIA (A100, H200) and AMD (MI300A) GPUs within the National Research Platform (NRP) ecosystem. A total of 15 open-source LLMs, ranging from 117 million to 90 billion parameters, are served using the vLLM framework. The QAic inference cards appears to be energy efficient and performs well in the energy efficiency metric in most cases. The findings offer insights into the potential of the Qualcomm Cloud AI 100 Ultra for high-performance computing (HPC) applications within the National Research Platform (NRP).
